The slow path is likely not one kernel alone: `F.linear` materializes a 5H projection tensor, the pack kernel re-reads it, `bmm` materializes the hidden output, then the norm/gate and final projection materialize again. I’m profiling one C128 Cauchy case and one C384 case to see which of those stages is worth attacking first.
